    "result_text": "Both tests pass and the build is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Structured address form \u2014 implemented\n\nThe request now accepts a structured address (`addressLine1`, optional `addressLine2`, plus the existing `city`/`postcode`), while the flat `address` string stays accepted for backward compatibility.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** (drives the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto`) \u2014 added `addressLine1` and `addressLine2` to `OwnerFields`, and **removed `address` from `required`** so a minimal owner can supply its address via either form (contract stays backward-compatible).\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` columns + accessors so the structured lines survive the persist/GET round-trip.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added `address_line_1`/`address_line_2` columns (tests run on hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist in the script).\n\n4. **`function/owner/Addresses.java`** \u2014 added `normalizeToNull` (stores an absent line as `null`) and `compose(...)`, which prefers the structured fields: normalized `addressLine1`, with a single space and normalized `addressLine2` appended when present, falling back to the normalized flat `address`.\n\n5. **`function/owner/BuildOwner.java`** (POST) \u2014 normalizes both lines and composes the effective `address` up front, so the required-field check rejects an address blank in *both* forms, and everything downstream that reads `owner.getAddress()` (household hash input, response, etc.) sees the composed structured value.\n\n6. **`function/owner/ApplyOwner.java`** (PUT) \u2014 same normalize-and-compose logic for parity.\n\n**Validation now:** an owner is valid with a non-blank `addressLine1` **or** a flat `address`, plus `city` (firstName/lastName/telephone unchanged).\n\n**Test result:** `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 both `coreNormalizesAndComposesStructuredAddress` (`\"10 king st\"` \u2192 `addressLine1` and `address` = `\"10 KING STREET\"`) and `functionalityStillAcceptsFlatAddress` pass; `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
